			"Message": "build(Sky): Bump Astro from 6.3.8 to 6.4.2\n\nUpgraded the Astro framework from version 6.3.8 to 6.4.2 to incorporate upstream bug fixes and performance improvements. This dependency update was triggered by automated Dependabot checks targeting the Land/Element/Sky package.\n\nNo breaking changes expected as this is a minor patch-level increment within the 6.x major version line. The upgrade maintains compatibility with existing build pipeline configurations including Playform compression plugins, Vite 8.0.14, and TypeScript 6.0.3.",
			"SHA": "8e20f8ed743e5724590d2cc9206193d63ef27fe8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-05-29T02:50:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "885f795ba6a66c3aad94a4ed97198e7ff71c5d55"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T18:38:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				34
			],
			"Message": "build(Sky): Extract bridge handlers into modular installers and harden build pipeline\n\nRefactor the monolithic `Bridge.ts` into discrete installer modules (Commands, EditorOperations, Scm, Webview, etc.) while introducing idempotent install guards and standardized error-surrounding try/catch blocks. The extraction preserves the existing dependency-injection shape (`Register`, `GetServices`, `Invoke`) so downstream call sites require no changes.\n\nStrengthen the Astro build pipeline: `BakeExtensionManifest` now scans `~/.land/extensions`, `~/.fiddee/extensions`, and `~/.vscode/extensions` with NLS-resolution fallback, writing both debug and production manifest paths while skipping stale cache hits. `CompressBundle` applies brotli compression (quality 11) to `_astro` and `Static/Application` artifacts, skipping files smaller than 1 KB or with < 5 % savings.\n\nHardened `astro.config.ts` with Vite define backfills for missing profile/color-scheme/terminal fields, performance-mark checkpoints spanning workbench boot phases, and robust extension auto-install logging. Output channel handlers now prefer `IOutputService.showChannel()` for targeted reveals, and notification relays drive `INotificationService.notify()` directly for production toast visibility.",
			"SHA": "e7bd6f220ab05562878801bac301061173aedf06"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1780160076626
}